hey guys it's Jonah here it's the  holiday season that also means the  season of soup has begun I love soup I'm  really excited to be sharing with you my  favorite soup recipes when you drink a  really good bowl of soup you will feel  good and you know that you're being  healthy as well so if you're looking to  lose weight or keep the weight off have  a bowl of soup prior to your meals it  has been proven to control hunger  resulting in you eating about 20% less  for your main meals if you don't like  your vegetables soup is also a great way  to add more vegetables into your diet I  used to date a guy who wouldn't touch  any vegetables it's impossible and I  found out that the only way he would  have his vegetables is if I were to  blend them and turn them into soup  totally work he would happily eat it the  entire serving and didn't even think of  them as vegetables so if your partner or  kids do not like their vegetables try  this trick here are three of my favorite  holiday season soup recipes there are so  delicious filling low in calories easy  to prep and made only with wholesome  ingredients it's the season of winter  squash right now so let's start by  making this rich bowl of coconut curry  pumpkin soup what you'll need are 1 kilo  of pumpkin roasted peeled and cubed 1  medium yellow onion diced 3 garlic  cloves minced 1 tablespoon of fresh  ginger minced half a cup of light  coconut milk 3 cups of vegetable stock 1  tablespoon of olive oil 1 teaspoon of  curry powder 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin 1/2  a teaspoon of turmeric 1 tsp of  coriander seed 1 tablespoon of fresh  lemon juice and salt and pepper to taste  in a large pot heat olive oil over  medium-high heat stir in the garlic  ginger and onion for one to two minutes  until slightly brown and fragrant add in  all the spices continue to stir for  another one minute until spices become  toasted and fragrant then add in the  pumpkin  vegetable stock and coconut milk bring  to a boil cover and simmer for another  10 minutes until pumpkin is tender turn  off the heat and puree all the  ingredients with a hand blender until  smooth seasoned with lemon salt and  pepper serve hot  I've garnished my coconut curry pumpkin  soup with pumpkin seeds and fresh  parsley the richness from the coconut  milk and the slight hint of spiciness  from the curry powder makes it a soul  warming dish winter squashes are also a  great way to thicken your soup without  adding that many calories so this one  large serving only has 130 calories be  sure to include this recipe for  Christmas on new year  the next recipe is the queen of comfort  food creamy mushroom soup the deep  earthy flavor is so soothing and hearty  the classic mushroom soup recipe it  tends to call for a lot of heavy cream  and can be packed with hidden calories  for my recipe we are going to give it a  slight twist and cook it without any  cream yet still maintaining its classic  flavor what you'll need are 500 gram of  fresh wild mushroom thinly sliced 3 cups  of cauliflower costly chopped 1 large  yellow onion diced 1 tbsp of olive oil 3  garlic cloves minced 4 cups of vegetable  stock 1 tablespoon of fresh lemon juice  and salt and pepper to taste  in a large pot add 2 cups of vegetable  stock and cauliflower bring to a boil  cover and simmer for about 10 minutes  and the cauliflower is very tender puree  with a hand blender until smooth and set  aside in a pan heats olive oil over  medium-high heat stir in the garlic  onion and mushroom saute for 5 to 10  minutes until onion and garlic are  golden brown and fragrant and mushrooms  are cooked through  then add 3/4 of the mushroom mixture and  the remaining 2 cups of vegetable stock  into the pureed cauliflower mixture  bring to a boil cover and simmer for 5  minutes until slightly thickened turn  off the heat  and puree all the ingredients with a  hand blender until smooth stir in the  remaining mushroom mixture and seasoned  with lemon salt and pepper serve hot so  the secret creamy ingredient is to add  pureed cauliflower into the mix is an  extremely good source of fiber which  means keeping you fuller for much longer  and it is also very low in calories with  only 72 calories per serving you don't  need a reason to enjoy a hearty bowl of  mushroom soup I like to have it  throughout the year so give this how  they recipe a try  and my final bowl of soup is filled with  sweet potato chunks black beans and  seasoned with lots of intense spices the  ingredients you'll need are 1 and a half  cup of sweet potato peeled and diced  into cubes one can offer black beans  rinsed and drained 1 medium yellow onion  diced 2 garlic cloves minced 1 TSP of  olive oil 1 TSP of cumin 1 teaspoon of  smoked paprika 1 tsp of coriander seed 2  cups of vegetable stock and salt and  pepper to taste  in a large pot heat olive oil over  medium-high heat add garlic and onion  and stir-fry very quickly  just until slightly brown and fragrant  then mix in the sweet potato black beans  and all the spices and continue to  stir-fry very quickly for another minute  then add the vegetable stock bring to a  boil cover and simmer for 15 to 20  minutes until SU potatoes are tender and  cooked through then turn off the heat  scoop out about one cup of sweet potato  and black beans mixture and set aside  puree the rest of the ingredients with a  hand blender until smooth  then turn the heat back on to low and  add back in the reserved 3 potatoes and  black beans season with salt and pepper  and cook very quickly for about 5  minutes just to heat the soup up this  bowl of soup is bursting with flavors  it's high in fiber and protein which  makes it a very satisfying meal we  member good food doesn't mean  complicated ingredients keep it simple  and wholesome to bring out the flavors  of each ingredient so to avoid over  indulging this holiday season and to  keep the weight off include soups into  your meals you can serve them as a  starter for your lunch or dinner or have  them as your afternoon snack soups are  so easy and convenient to make in large  batches which also makes it a really  good food for parties make them and let  me know which is your favorite so  warming soup in the comments below and  be sure to have a beautiful holiday  season we can loved once all the best  you  you
 

